{
  "0": "For all four datasets, condition each HSTU attention gate on the current token: replace gate(attn_out) with value=Wv(attn_out), gate=Wg(normed), and residual dropout(value*SiLU(gate)). This may preserve current-item intent while selectively incorporating history. Retain causal attention, FFN, embeddings, cumulative observed-position IDs, readout, scoring, loss and optimizer. Train one model per category and synchronize architecture loading through the predictor writer.",
  "1": "For all four datasets, replace each position's encoder-state readout with 0.75*h_t + 0.25*p_t, where p_t is a normalized causal mean of nonpadding states h_j weighted by exp(-(t-j)/4), j<=t. This may stabilize short-history representations while emphasizing recent interests. Retain cumulative observed-position IDs, truncation, HSTU topology, embeddings, scoring, loss and optimizer. Apply identically during training and inference; read the final real position.",
  "2": "For all four datasets, apply smooth norm compression to tied item embeddings: e_eff=e/sqrt(1+||e||²), with padding exactly zero. Use the same transformation for history and candidate lookups, retaining dimension 64 and the existing input multiplier. Unlike hard unit normalization, this preserves magnitude differences among small embeddings while limiting large norms. Keep HSTU topology, positions, history policy, dot-product scoring, loss and optimizer fixed; synchronize predictor behavior.",
  "3": "For all four datasets, replace the pairwise loss with margin-one logistic ranking loss: softplus(1-(positive_score-negative_score)), averaged over the same valid target positions. Requiring greater positive-negative separation may improve top-10 discrimination without changing sampled pairs or adding another scorer. Preserve embeddings, HSTU architecture, cumulative positions, scoring/readout, optimizer, sampling and training schedule. Retain exactly one trained checkpoint per category."
}
